# ADR-001: Use JavaScript/Node across all tiers

## Status
Proposed

## Context
No implementation exists yet, and a language needs to be picked before any
boilerplate work (like the landing page) can continue consistently. The
repo's CI templates only cover Python and Java, but neither was a hard
requirement.

## Decision
Build the project in JavaScript/Node.js across all four tiers (Presentation,
Service, Domain, Data). This keeps one language, one dependency file, and
one CI pipeline for the whole project instead of splitting the stack.

## Consequences
- Domain-layer math (volatility, diversification score) will be written in
  plain JS rather than relying on a numerical library like NumPy.
- CI had to be hand-written for Node since no JS template was provided in
  the repo, unlike the existing Python/Java templates.
- If a feature later needs heavier statistical or ML tooling, a separate
  Python service may be added, but that is not planned as a starting
  requirement.
